  "prompt": "/deep-research Limiting to member localities of the Central Shenandoah Planning District Commission with populations under 30,000 according to 2020 U.S. Census, which one's had more than a thousand National Forest Permits issued as reported by Virginia DWR for fiscal year 2020?",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Limiting to member localities of the Central Shenandoah Planning District Commission with populations under 30,000 according to 2020 U.S. Census, which one's had more than a thousand National Forest Permits issued as reported by Virginia DWR for fiscal year 2020?",
  "answer": "Now I have all the data. Let me cross-reference the CSPDC localities with populations under 30,000 and their National Forest Permit counts.\n\n**CSPDC Member Localities — Cross-Reference**\n\n| Locality | 2020 Census Pop | Pop <30k? | Nat'l Forest Permits (FY2020) | >1,000? |\n|----------|-----------------|-----------|-------------------------------|---------|\n| **Counties** | | | | |\n| Augusta County | 77,487 | No | 4,381 | — |\n| Bath County | 4,209 | **Yes** | 962 | No |\n| Highland County | 2,232 | **Yes** | 258 | No |\n| **Rockbridge County** | **22,650** | **Yes** | **1,121** | **Yes** ✓ |\n| Rockingham County | 83,757 | No | 5,461 | — |\n| **Independent Cities** | | | | |\n| Buena Vista | 6,641 | **Yes** | 785 | No |\n| Harrisonburg | 51,814 | No | 2,171 | — |\n| Lexington | 7,320 | **Yes** | 908 | No |\n| **Staunton** | **25,750** | **Yes** | **2,112** | **Yes** ✓ |\n| **Waynesboro** | **22,196** | **Yes** | **1,577** | **Yes** ✓ |\n\n## Answer\n\n**Three** CSPDC member localities with 2020 Census populations under 30,000 had more than 1,000 National Forest Permits issued in FY2020:\n\n1. **Rockbridge County** — 22,650 population, **1,121 permits**\n2. **Staunton** — 25,750 population, **2,112 permits**\n3. **Waynesboro** — 22,196 population, **1,577 permits**\n\nBath County (4,209 pop, 962 permits), Highland County (2,232 pop, 258 permits), Buena Vista (6,641 pop, 785 permits), and Lexington (7,320 pop, 908 permits) all fell short of the 1,000-permit threshold.\n\n## Sources\n- CSPDC member localities: [cspdc.org/about](https://cspdc.org/about), [waynesboro.va.us/344/Central-Shenandoah-Planning-District-Com](https://www.waynesboro.va.us/344/Central-Shenandoah-Planning-District-Com)\n- 2020 Census populations: U.S. Census Bureau Decennial Census 2020 (via Census QuickFacts, Census Reporter, Wikipedia citations)\n- Virginia DWR FY2020 National Forest Permit data: [dwr.virginia.gov/data/licenses](https://dwr.virginia.gov/data/licenses) — `fishing-and-hunting-license-sales-FY2020.csv` (license code 472 = National Forest Permit), saved as `/home/ubuntu/virginia_national_forest_permits_fy2020.csv`",
  "answer_chars": 2107,
  "expected_answer": "Rockbridge County, City of Staunton, City of Waynesboro",
